- How to handle late-arriving data and replays without breaking lineage?
- How to enforce tenant isolation at storage and compute layers?

Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical implementation of data quality, lineage, and drift management in a multi-tenant GCP environment—critical skills for enterprise data engineering roles.

Key Concepts
- Per-tenant data contracts with field-level validation constraints
- Streaming quality enforcement using Dataflow templates
- End-to-end lineage tracking via Data Catalog integration
- Schema drift detection and automated remediation workflows
- 24-hour rollback capabilities with tenant-isolated backfill strategies
- Quality monitoring and alerting through Looker dashboards

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow DoFn for contract validation (simplified)
function validateRecord(record, contract) {
  const errors = [];

  // Required field validation
  for (const field of contract.requiredFields) {
    if (!record.hasOwnProperty(field)) {
      errors.push(`Missing required field: ${field}`);
    }
  }

  // Type and constraint validation
  for (const [field, constraint] of Object.entries(contract.constraints)) {
    if (record[field] !== undefined) {
      if (!validateType(record[field], constraint.type)) {
        errors.push(`Invalid type for ${field}`);
      }
      if (!validateConstraint(record[field], constraint)) {
        errors.push(`Constraint violation for ${field}`);
      }
    }
  }

  return {
    isValid: errors.length === 0,
    record: errors.length === 0 ? record : null,
    errors: errors.length > 0 ? errors : null
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests end-to-end real-time data engineering competencies on GCP, including multi-tenant isolation, dynamic schema evolution, data contracts, and rollback semantics, plus cross-cloud replication and testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time ingestion with Pub/Sub and Dataflow templates
- Per-tenant isolation using partitioned BigQuery datasets
- Central schema registry in Data Catalog for dynamic evolution
- End-to-end lineage and data contracts
- 24-hour per-tenant rollback via BigQuery time travel
- Cross-region replication to Snowflake via Snowpipe

## Code Example

```java
// Dataflow pipeline with tenant isolation and schema validation
public class TenantPipeline {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        PipelineOptions options = PipelineOptionsFactory.fromArgs(args).create();
        Pipeline pipeline = Pipeline.create(options);

        pipeline
            .apply("Read from Pub/Sub", PubsubIO.readMessagesWithAttributes()
                .fromSubscription(options.getSubscription()))
            .apply("Extract tenant ID", ParDo.of(new ExtractTenantDoFn()))
            .apply("Validate against schema", ParDo.of(new SchemaValidationDoFn()))
            .apply("Write to tenant BigQuery", new TenantBigQueryWrite());

        pipeline.run();
    }
}
```
